    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n13 The Wooden Building is well presented one bedroom apartment located in the heart of temple bar, one of Dublin City Centre's most historic and exciting areas to live. Surrounded by endless amenities and public transport, this is an ideal apartment for those looking for a City Centre base. \n\nThe apartment consists of a warm and welcoming entrance hall giving access to the bright and spacious living/dining room, while also offering views over the communal garden, and a well-appointed kitchen. The double bedroom can be accessed from the hall and has generous built-in wardrobes. The bathroom is tiled and accessed from the hallway. \n\nThis chic apartment is situated in the heart of Temple Bar along the banks of the River Liffey, in one of Dublin most sought-after and historical areas of the city. The unrivalled location cannot go unmentioned, as there are countless Dublin Bus routes, taxi ranks, Dublin Bike stations, LUAS lines, and train stations all within walking distance. Such a central location also puts you in walking distance of Trinity College, St Stephens Green, Grafton Street and countless restaurants and cafes."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 0.977m x 2.743m\nA warm and welcoming entrance hall.\n\nLiving/Dining Room - 4.348m x 3.075m\nBright and spacious living/dining room with laminate wooden flooring and an open kitchen.\n\nKitchen - 0.815m x 2.472m\nWell-appointed modern kitchen off the living/dining room with a tiled splashback, ample storage in the floor and wall-mounted cupboards, and plumbing for a washing machine.\n\nBedroom - 4.130m x 2.918m\nGenerous double bedroom with laminate wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes, and a large window flooding the room with natural light.\n\nBathroom - 1.671m x 2.077m\nMain bathroom with a WC, WHB, bath, and overhead shower attachment.\n\n"
      },
      {
